Carafe: with d3d9.effectPassMerge on top of d3d9.effectThread, the effect worker joins passes. A game that ends a
pass and begins the same pass again, with only parameter changes, draws, vertex and index streams and states the pass
does not set in between, gets the pass kept open and its changed parameters committed instead of every state of the
pass applied again. The states a pass sets are recorded on the downstream front end while the effect library applies
them; anything else ends the pass as the game asked, and so does every wait for the queue, so the game never sees an
effect left in a pass. With the profiler on, the passes begun and joined per frame and what ended the joins are logged
every 600 presents.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

